Forró Box @VERSION@ — Windows x64
@UNDERLINE@

Contents
  ForroBox.vst3   the VST3 instrument (a folder — copy the whole folder)
  ForroBox.exe    the standalone application
  LICENSE         GNU GPL v3 — source: https://github.com/dobidu/forrobox (tag @TAG@)
  NOTICE.md       third-party licences (JUCE, fonts, samples); font licences in licenses\

Requirements
  Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, and a VST3 host (Ableton Live, Reaper, Bitwig, FL Studio, Cubase...).
  Nothing else to install: the C++ runtime is built in.

Install the VST3
  1. Copy the whole ForroBox.vst3 folder into
       C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3\
     (or any folder your DAW is set to scan for VST3 plugins).
  2. Rescan plugins in your DAW. It is listed as "Forro Box" (no accent), an instrument.
  3. Load it on a MIDI/instrument track and press play. A fresh instance loads CAMPINA GRANDE.

Standalone
  Double-click ForroBox.exe. Choose your audio device under Options > Audio/MIDI Settings.

Not code-signed: Windows SmartScreen may warn about ForroBox.exe. Choose "More info" > "Run anyway".
